.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause
.Dd October 7, 2026
.Dt NDBECTL 8
.Os NeoDarwin
.Sh NAME
.Nm ndbectl
.Nd manage ZFS boot environments
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl p Ar pool
.Cm list | create Ar new Op Ar origin | Cm activate Oo Fl t Oc Ar be | Cm mount Ar be dir | Cm umount Ar be | Cm destroy Ar be
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Boot environments are the datasets
.Ar pool Ns /ROOT/ Ns Ar be ,
as
.Xr bectl 8
makes them.
.Bl -tag -width activate
.It Cm list
Each BE with flags
.Li N
(booted),
.Li R
(the pool's
.Li bootfs ) ,
.Li T
(the pool's
.Li org.neodarwin:bootonce ) .
.It Cm create Ar new Op Ar origin
Snapshot
.Ar origin
(default: the booted BE) and clone it.
.It Cm activate Oo Fl t Oc Ar be
Set
.Li bootfs ;
with
.Fl t ,
boot
.Ar be
once
.Pq Li org.neodarwin:bootonce ,
which zfs.kext clears as it boots it.
.It Cm mount Ar be dir , Cm umount Ar be
Mount a BE that isn't booted.
.It Cm destroy Ar be
Destroy a BE that is neither booted nor active, and its origin snapshot.
.El
.Pp
On a disk whose ESP has per-BE kernels
.Pq Li be= No in Pa boot.cfg ,
the loader pins the root to the BE whose kernel it loads, and
.Xr ndpkg-system 8
chooses it.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ndpkg-system 8 ,
.Xr zfs 8 ,
.Xr zpool 8
.Sh HISTORY
P3-03; in the base since P2-03, for
.Xr bectl 8
and
.Xr zfsbootcfg 8 .
